    "last_attempts_log": [
      {
        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 56.441,
        "asr_text": "Imagine you are reading, studying, or working. Your phone is on the desk. You do not touch it. You do not even look at the screen. Then comes a short notification sound. You keep your eyes on your work, but your attention may have already moved. A study published in 2022 tested this idea with 73 university students. They completed a simple visual task many times. Some rounds included a phone notification sound. Other rounds included a neutral sound. The students did not look at or touch a phone during the task. Even so, they answered more slowly after hearing the notification sound. A brainwave signal was also larger. The researchers understood this as a sign that the students needed extra mental effort to keep working.",
