        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 41.101,
        "asr_text": "This may help explain why checking a phone can feel difficult to stop. In a 2018 survey, 72% of U.S. teenagers said they often or sometimes checked messages or notifications soon after waking up. About four in 10 said they felt worried, upset, or lonely when their phone was not nearby. A majority also felt they should reply quickly to messages. These answers describe teenagers' experiences. They do not prove that phones caused those feelings, but they show how closely phone checking can be tied to daily life.",
        "asr_text_length": 514,
        "max_len": 569,
